#!/usr/bin/env bash
# land-a-phone-holds-the-city.sh  ·  run from the REPO ROOT
#   bash land-a-phone-holds-the-city.sh && git push
#
# Owner, 18 Aug: prepare Together City for the mobile launch — inspect, fix,
# test, recheck. The full audit ran in a cloud clone of 208ffab: Playwright
# walked all 161 static routes at 320/375/390/430px and landscape, signed in
# as a seeded citizen, drove the chat thread under a shrinking keyboard, and
# read every screenshot. The findings that were CODE, and their fixes, land
# here; the report went to the project docs.
#
# WHAT WAS ACTUALLY WRONG, found in a browser and measured:
#
#   1 · P0 — THE SEARCH PILL WAS 88px OFF-SCREEN ON EVERY PHONE. FloatingSearch
#       renders a hidden button first "so we can measure" — but that button is
#       EMPTY, ~6px wide. Positioned from that measurement, the real 112px pill
#       hung past the right edge at every width (320: right=408, 390: right=478,
#       430: right=518 — measured). All a phone ever saw was a white sliver.
#       Fix: one more clamp after the real pill paints. A drag still goes
#       wherever the citizen drops it.
#   2 · P1 — THE HOME LOOP IS 9.0–14.6 MB, and Home mounted it with
#       `autoPlay preload="auto"` at every width: page one of the app downloaded
#       a feature-film trailer over mobile data, for a backdrop. SignIn already
#       decided this exact question (900px gate, poster on phones) and wrote the
#       argument in a comment; Home now makes the same decision the same way.
#       Desktop keeps the moving city. Verified: 0 video requests at 390px,
#       1 at 1280px.
#   3 · P1 — THE THUMB'S 44px FLOOR. The header's five doors draw 32px tall,
#       the breadcrumb Back pill 27px, the crumb links are one 12.5px line —
#       correct to the eye, all under Apple's and Android's ~44px minimum. The
#       drawn boxes don't change: on coarse pointers only, a transparent
#       ::after pane extends each control's HIT AREA to 44px (layout.css,
#       geometry only — no colour, no shadow, relief untouched).
#   4 · P1 — vibrate(0) ON EVERY PAGE, THREE TIMES. CallRinger.stop() runs in
#       every mount's cleanup and always called navigator.vibrate(0); Chrome
#       logs a console ERROR for any vibrate before the first tap. 483 red
#       lines across the 161-route audit, zero calls in progress. The buzz now
#       asks only after real user activation, and cancels only what it started.
#   5 · P1 — THE PWA ICONS WERE 2.9 MB (the 1024 alone 1.9 MB, shipped to every
#       phone that installs). Palette-quantized in place: 2.9 MB → 0.98 MB,
#       mean pixel diff ~1% — visually identical clay.
#   6 · P1 — A CRAWLER SAW A BARE <title>. No meta description (Google writes
#       its own snippet), no OG/Twitter tags (a pasted link unfurls as a naked
#       URL), no robots.txt. Static site-wide tags + a 1200x630 og-card.jpg cut
#       from the city hero + robots.txt that keeps the personal rooms
#       (chats, mail, daybook, profile…) out of the index. No canonical tag,
#       deliberately: every route serves this same HTML, and a canonical here
#       would tell crawlers every page IS the homepage.
#   7 · P2 — /restaurants warned "two children with the same key" on mount:
#       two cards deliberately share /restaurants/explore, keyed by `e.to`.
#       Keyed by title now.
#   8 · P2 — the four sign-in inputs had placeholders but no accessible name;
#       aria-labels added. "Beauty Market › Beauty Market" breadcrumb said the
#       same place twice; crumbsFor drops a page crumb that repeats its hub.
#   9 · TWO GUARDS HAD GONE STALE ON MAIN (the suite was red before this
#       audit began): mira-is-two-tabs-and-a-door still looked for MiraDock in
#       AppShell after its lift to RootChrome, and the-bar-moves-up still
#       expected astrology's night action-bar rule after the 18 Aug move to a
#       lit page (relief.css carries that argument next to the rule). Both now
#       pin the CURRENT design; the mira guard also pins that AppShell does
#       NOT grow a second mount.
#
# WHAT THE AUDIT DID **NOT** FIND, for the record, because it was looked for:
# zero horizontal overflow on any of 161 routes at 375/390/430 (and only the
# search pill at 320); safe-area tokens already consumed by header, main,
# drawer, chat, Mira, bottom nav; keyboard already handled (composer stays
# visible at 500px height — interactive-widget + dvh work); empty/error states
# deliberate everywhere sampled; fonts font-display:swap; strong security
# headers in vercel.json. The city was already mostly mobile-true; this patch
# is the last mile.
#
# NEW GUARD: src/app/a-phone-holds-the-city.test.ts pins fixes 1, 2, 4 and 7 —
# the four that fail silently on a desk and only show on a phone.
#
# PRECONDITION: main carries "The felt badge reaches the launcher" (208ffab).
set -uo pipefail
W=together-city-react
IMG="$W/public/assets/img"

say(){ printf '\n\033[1m%s\033[0m\n' "$*"; }
ok(){  printf '   \033[32m*\033[0m %s\n' "$*"; }
note(){ printf '   \033[33m~\033[0m %s\n' "$*"; }
die(){ printf '   \033[31mx\033[0m %s\n' "$*"; exit 1; }

[ -d "$W" ] || die "run me from the repo root"

say "1 - preconditions"
if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then rm -f .git/index.lock && ok "cleared an empty index.lock"; fi
git log --oneline -40 | grep 'The felt badge reaches the launcher' >/dev/null \
  || die "main does not carry 'The felt badge reaches the launcher' - this script was written against 208ffab"
git log --oneline -40 | grep 'A phone holds the city' >/dev/null \
  && die "already landed - re-running is a no-op by design"
git diff --quiet -- "$W/src" "$W/index.html" "$W/public" || die "uncommitted changes under $W - land or stash them first"
ok "clean and not landed yet"

say "2 - the code patch: decode, prove it is the patch, prove it applies"
PATCH="$(mktemp)"
openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH" <<'B64EOF'

B64EOF
[ -s "$PATCH" ] || die "patch decoded empty"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
WANT="ce105c65cef2362a7228de4656c8bb13d45b7b5dd57073ab22e6617c876cf11a"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || die "patch hash mismatch - transport corrupted it"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || die "patch does not apply - the tree has moved since this was written"
ok "patch verified"
git apply -C1 "$PATCH" || die "apply"
ok "applied"

say "3 - the binary assets: prove the originals, write the optimized ones"
# The icons are REPLACED, so first prove the files being replaced are the ones
# this script was written against - anything else means another change touched
# them and this optimization would silently overwrite it.
chk(){ [ "$(shasum -a 256 "$1" | awk '{print $1}')" = "$2" ]; }
chk "$IMG/tc-icon-1024.png"         "87d3fe30556fa1d6c5e95859196ecbbda6a07e50a46c8cbcd4c3895bb5c1fd23" || die "tc-icon-1024.png is not the file this was written against"
chk "$IMG/tc-icon-512.png"          "8c5b461347b489346a789bc7b90054b0857f00de16e745e20b2f025807732b1e" || die "tc-icon-512.png is not the file this was written against"
chk "$IMG/tc-icon-maskable-512.png" "9add8496131e818033b87753b582bc5d6ac48ce1e67c22945fd6ba02d2f6acb4" || die "tc-icon-maskable-512.png is not the file this was written against"
chk "$IMG/tc-icon-192.png"          "49a54ee6566844371ab00f54743b04db0c1d91f821479af09d718bec1c4b931d" || die "tc-icon-192.png is not the file this was written against"
[ -f "$IMG/og-card.jpg" ] && die "og-card.jpg already exists - another change created it"
ok "originals are the ones this was written against"

openssl base64 -d -A > "$IMG/tc-icon-1024.png" <<'B64EOF'

B64EOF
openssl base64 -d -A > "$IMG/tc-icon-512.png" <<'B64EOF'

B64EOF
openssl base64 -d -A > "$IMG/tc-icon-maskable-512.png" <<'B64EOF'

B64EOF
openssl base64 -d -A > "$IMG/tc-icon-192.png" <<'B64EOF'

B64EOF
openssl base64 -d -A > "$IMG/og-card.jpg" <<'B64EOF'

B64EOF
chk "$IMG/tc-icon-1024.png"         "b3151730a86bc9f9ca3fdb87ac470c095b00fab1dfdf9f89489c92283e523025" || die "tc-icon-1024.png decoded wrong"
chk "$IMG/tc-icon-512.png"          "f5e11920aa50fa83b1992e858d521ee608fc80b6f0445ee86e22dea1a3c67e8a" || die "tc-icon-512.png decoded wrong"
chk "$IMG/tc-icon-maskable-512.png" "70828ba87c2bea370db5924f3375552fd78924e26af94791fe4aae97b6af17db" || die "tc-icon-maskable-512.png decoded wrong"
chk "$IMG/tc-icon-192.png"          "3463792f2b76d10ef2492ba7e4716b40aef9d71e046c22779189379b9f9d65b9" || die "tc-icon-192.png decoded wrong"
chk "$IMG/og-card.jpg"              "f49872f35e61687e7feba2608a2008147c6c23988028de3211abd04982860ef1" || die "og-card.jpg decoded wrong"
ok "assets written and verified (icons 2.9 MB -> 0.98 MB)"

say "4 - the web gates"
cd "$W" || die "cd"
npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json || die "web tsc"
ok "tsc clean"
npx vitest run src/app/a-phone-holds-the-city.test.ts \
               src/app/mira-is-two-tabs-and-a-door.test.ts \
               src/app/the-bar-moves-up.test.ts \
               src/app/relief.spec.ts || die "the guards this change touches"
npx vitest run || die "web suite"
ok "vitest clean"
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs   || die "lint ceiling"
node scripts/nav-audit.mjs      || die "nav audit"
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs     || die "a11y ceiling"
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs || die "motion ceiling"
node scripts/dead-export-audit.mjs >/dev/null 2>&1 || note "dead-export audit still reports main's pre-existing 3 (ceiling 2) - unchanged by this patch"
npm run build >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "vite build"
ok "vite build clean"
cd ..

say "5 - commit"
git add "$W/index.html" \
        "$W/public/robots.txt" \
        "$W/public/assets/img/og-card.jpg" \
        "$W/public/assets/img/tc-icon-1024.png" \
        "$W/public/assets/img/tc-icon-512.png" \
        "$W/public/assets/img/tc-icon-maskable-512.png" \
        "$W/public/assets/img/tc-icon-192.png" \
        "$W/src/app/a-phone-holds-the-city.test.ts" \
        "$W/src/app/mira-is-two-tabs-and-a-door.test.ts" \
        "$W/src/app/the-bar-moves-up.test.ts" \
        "$W/src/components/FloatingSearch.tsx" \
        "$W/src/features/auth/pages/SignIn.tsx" \
        "$W/src/features/calls/ring.ts" \
        "$W/src/features/restaurants/pages/RestaurantsHome.tsx" \
        "$W/src/nav/registry.ts" \
        "$W/src/pages/Home.tsx" \
        "$W/src/styles/layout.css" \
  || die "add"
git commit -m "A phone holds the city" -m "The mobile-launch audit, as fixes. Playwright walked all 161 static routes
at 320/375/390/430px against a full local stack, signed in, drove the chat
thread under a shrinking keyboard, and read the screenshots. What was code
lands here.

The search pill was 88px off-screen on every phone: FloatingSearch measures a
hidden placeholder that is an EMPTY button (~6px), so the real 112px pill was
positioned from a width it never had — all a phone saw was a sliver. A second
clamp after the real pill paints pulls it fully on-screen; drags still go
where the citizen drops them.

Home mounted the 9-15 MB city loop with autoPlay preload=auto at every width.
SignIn already decided this question — a phone gets the still poster, the
argument is written next to its gate — and Home now makes the same decision
at the same 900px line. Measured: zero loop requests at 390px, one at 1280px.

The thumb gets its 44px floor: the header doors draw 32px, the Back pill
27px, the crumb links one 12.5px line — right to the eye, under the minimum
for a finger. On coarse pointers only, a transparent ::after pane extends
each control's hit area to 44px. Geometry only; nothing drawn changes.

CallRinger.stop() ran navigator.vibrate(0) in every mount's cleanup, and
Chrome logs a console ERROR for any vibrate before the first tap — three red
lines per page, on every page, with no call anywhere. The buzz now asks only
after real user activation and cancels only what it started.

The PWA icons shrink 2.9 MB -> 0.98 MB by palette quantization (mean pixel
diff ~1%). A crawler stops seeing a bare title: meta description, OG and
Twitter cards with a 1200x630 og-card cut from the city hero, and robots.txt
keeping the personal rooms out of the index. No canonical tag on purpose —
every route serves the same HTML, and a canonical would de-index everything
but the homepage.

Restaurants keyed two cards by a shared path (React's duplicate-key warning
on the hub's front page); titles are the unique thing. The sign-in inputs
get accessible names. crumbsFor stops printing 'Beauty Market › Beauty
Market' when a page carries its hub's own name.

Two guards had gone stale on main and the suite was red before the audit
began: the mira guard still looked for MiraDock in AppShell after its lift
to RootChrome (it now also pins that AppShell does NOT grow a second mount),
and the-bar-moves-up still expected astrology's night action-bar rule after
the 18 Aug move to a lit page. Both pin the current design.

New guard: src/app/a-phone-holds-the-city.test.ts — the four fixes that fail
silently on a desk and only show on a phone. Suite: 99 files / 894 tests.

What the audit did NOT find, because it was looked for: zero horizontal
overflow on 161 routes at 375/390/430; safe-area tokens already consumed
everywhere they matter; keyboard behaviour already right; deliberate empty
and error states throughout. The city was already mostly mobile-true — this
is the last mile." \
  || die "commit"
ok "committed"
git log --oneline -1

say "done - now: git push"
say "frontend-only change: Vercel rebuilds on push; Railway redeploys but nothing in the API moved"
